{
  "slug": "clarity",
  "name": "Clarity",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Clarity explains what Claude Code built in language anyone can understand. You can ask Claude to explain things, but that only works when you know what to ask about. Clarity walks through everything systematically, catching changes you didn't notice and decisions you didn't realise were made. Run /clarity:explain for a quick answer. Run /clarity:session after a build. Run /clarity:project for the full picture. Every explanation ends with prompts for your next se...",
  "longDescription": "Ships **3 skills** and **5 commands**.\n\n- **Skills** (3): `explanation-frameworks` (Defines how Clarity translates technical concepts into plain language), `review-methodology` (Core methodology governing how Clarity conducts plain-language reviews of AI development work), `scope-management` (Defines how Clarity manages review scope for sessions and projects of varying sizes)\n- **Commands** (5): `config` (Set where Clarity saves review files), `explain` (No argument = explain last message), `help` (Display Clarity command reference and disclaimer), `project` (Summarise a project in plain language), `session` (Summarise this session in plain language)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install clarity@claude-community` from `ashbysystems/clarity`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 3,
    "command": 5
  },
